Parent: 1444

## Context
Author request (2026-11-02), third of the three principles split out of 1444:
accept an explicit "I cannot measure this" when evidence is insufficient, to
reduce pressure to invent results.

## Scope
Measurement outputs distinguish measured, derived, estimated, and unavailable
results. An unavailable result states the missing evidence, what was attempted,
and what would permit measurement. Missing access or failed execution must not
be reported as zero, absence, or an all-clear. Integrate into the maintained
authoring guidance (diagnosis discipline in rules/workflow.md) and demonstrate
on one existing scripted workflow (selected by the 1444 inventory).

## Relevant files
- rules/coding-python.md
- skills/harness-doctor/references/authoring-skills.md
- skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md, if present; otherwise locate its maintained source
- rules/workflow.md (diagnosis discipline)
- One existing scripted skill and its helper, selected after inventory

## Exit criteria
- [x] The maintained authoring guidance states the measured / derived /
      estimated / unavailable taxonomy and the rule that missing access or
      failed execution is never reported as zero, absence, or an all-clear.
      Done: authoring-skills.md § Toolkit principles (310223ae, b5c1383a).
- [ ] An unavailable-measurement case and a positive control are demonstrated,
      showing that missing evidence cannot produce a fabricated result or
      all-clear.
- [ ] Run checks appropriate to changed files; regenerate generated guidance
      or catalogs only when their sources change.

## Verification
Bounded procedural walkthrough and reproducible examples for the pilot. Add
behavioral tests only where script behavior changes; do not pin prose with
wording tests or introduce a new enforcement guard merely to police the
principle.
